※ pl4g-test: compile=ok opt=0,1
※ pl4g-test: run=native,qemu exit=1
※ pl4g-test: diag=none

※ And the other half: where the answer is read, the call is made and what it
※ wrote is what the program goes on with.  The same program as the one beside
※ this, with the condition the other way round.

@[inline(never)]
fn three() → 〈u8, u8, u8〉:
    〈1u8, 2u8, 3u8〉

fn pick(c: bool) → u8:
    let t: 〈u8, u8, u8〉 = three()
    if c:
        t⟦0⟧
    else:
        7u8

@[startup]
fn main() → u6:
    ⎕narrow(pick(true), ⌜u6⌝) ?? 1u6
